  1207→/* Convert a series of STRING, WSTRING, STRING16, STRING32 and/or
  1208→   UTF8STRING tokens into a tree, performing string constant
  1209→   concatenation.  TOK is the first of these.  VALP is the location to
  1210→   write the string into.  OBJC_STRING indicates whether an '@' token
  1211→   preceded the incoming token (in that case, the strings can either
  1212→   be ObjC strings, preceded by a single '@', or normal strings, not
  1213→   preceded by '@'.  The result will be a CPP_OBJC_STRING).  Returns
  1214→   the CPP token type of the result (CPP_STRING, CPP_WSTRING,
  1215→   CPP_STRING32, CPP_STRING16, CPP_UTF8STRING, or CPP_OBJC_STRING).
  1216→
